---
import Figure from "./Figure.astro";

/* The "growth brake": FGFR3 stuck on in a growth-plate cell, and CNP easing
   it through NPR-B. With `medicines`, numbered markers show where the growth
   drugs act, explained in a list under the drawing. */
interface Props {
  caption: string;
  medicines?: boolean;
}
const { caption, medicines = false } = Astro.props;
const id = medicines ? "brake-meds" : "brake";
---
<Figure
  caption={caption}
  credit="Original diagram for this guide, simplified from the growth-plate signalling described in Ornitz & Legeai-Mallet, *Developmental Dynamics* 2017, and the International Consensus Statement, 2022. Not to scale."
>
  <svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 360 316" role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-title ${id}-desc`}>
    <title id={`${id}-title`}>How the achondroplasia growth brake works{medicines ? ", and where the medicines act" : ""}</title>
    <desc id={`${id}-desc`}>
      A growth-plate cartilage cell. Outside the cell, the growth factor FGF binds the FGFR3 receptor in the cell
      membrane. Inside, FGFR3's switch is stuck on in achondroplasia and sends too much STAT1 and MAPK signal, so
      growth-plate cells multiply and mature less and the arms, legs and skull base grow less. On the right, the
      body's own CNP binds a second receptor, NPR-B, which blocks the MAPK signal and eases the brake.
      {medicines && " Marker 1 is on CNP: vosoritide and navepegritide are long-lasting forms of CNP. Marker 2 is on FGFR3's switch: infigratinib and dabogratinib (TYRA-300) are pills that block it."}
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id={`${id}-arrow`} viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z" class="dia__arrowhead" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <text class="dia__zone" x="12" y="20">OUTSIDE THE CELL</text>
    <circle class="dia__fgf" cx="86" cy="42" r="6" />
    <circle class="dia__fgf" cx="100" cy="42" r="6" />
    <text class="dia__label" x="74" y="46" text-anchor="end">FGF</text>
    <path class="dia__cnp" d="M262,33 L271,42 L262,51 L253,42 Z" />
    <text class="dia__label" x="278" y="46">CNP</text>

    <rect class="dia__membrane" x="0" y="72" width="360" height="20" />
    <text class="dia__small" x="180" y="86" text-anchor="middle">Cell membrane</text>

    <rect class="dia__fgfr3" x="83" y="54" width="20" height="66" rx="6" />
    <text class="dia__label dia__label--strong" x="111" y="64">FGFR3</text>
    <rect class="dia__nprb" x="252" y="54" width="20" height="66" rx="6" />
    <text class="dia__label dia__label--strong" x="244" y="64" text-anchor="end">NPR-B</text>

    <text class="dia__zone" x="180" y="112" text-anchor="middle">INSIDE THE CELL</text>
    <rect class="dia__switch" x="32" y="120" width="122" height="23" rx="5" />
    <text class="dia__on" x="93" y="136" text-anchor="middle">Switch stuck ON</text>

    <path class="dia__arrow" d="M78,143 L64,176" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`} />
    <path class="dia__arrow" d="M110,143 L182,176" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`} />
    <rect class="dia__box" x="14" y="178" width="98" height="40" rx="6" />
    <text class="dia__label dia__label--strong" x="63" y="195" text-anchor="middle">STAT1</text>
    <text class="dia__small" x="63" y="210" text-anchor="middle">signal</text>
    <rect class="dia__box" x="136" y="178" width="98" height="40" rx="6" />
    <text class="dia__label dia__label--strong" x="185" y="195" text-anchor="middle">MAPK</text>
    <text class="dia__small" x="185" y="210" text-anchor="middle">signal</text>

    <path class="dia__block" d="M262,120 V198 H240" />
    <path class="dia__block" d="M240,188 V208" />
    <text class="dia__small" x="270" y="150">Blocks MAPK,</text>
    <text class="dia__small" x="270" y="166">easing the</text>
    <text class="dia__small" x="270" y="182">brake</text>

    <path class="dia__arrow" d="M63,218 V250" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`} />
    <path class="dia__arrow" d="M185,218 V250" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`} />
    <rect class="dia__outcome" x="14" y="252" width="332" height="52" rx="8" />
    <text class="dia__label dia__label--strong" x="180" y="273" text-anchor="middle">Growth-plate cells multiply and mature less</text>
    <text class="dia__small" x="180" y="292" text-anchor="middle">so the arms, legs and skull base grow less</text>

    {medicines && (
      <g>
        <circle class="dia__badge" cx="332" cy="42" r="11" />
        <text class="dia__badge-num" x="332" y="47" text-anchor="middle">1</text>
        <circle class="dia__badge" cx="16" cy="131" r="11" />
        <text class="dia__badge-num" x="16" y="136" text-anchor="middle">2</text>
      </g>
    )}
  </svg>
  {medicines && (
    <ol class="dia-legend">
      <li><strong>Vosoritide</strong> (daily injection) and <strong>navepegritide</strong> (weekly injection) are long-lasting forms of CNP, so the brake stays eased for longer.</li>
      <li><strong>Infigratinib</strong> and <strong>dabogratinib (TYRA-300)</strong> are pills, still in trials or under review, that block FGFR3's switch inside the cell, quieting the brake at its source.</li>
    </ol>
  )}
</Figure>
